     "They believed He was truly divine and truly human.",
     "But explaining how His divinity and humanity were united became a major theological challenge.",
     "Church leaders gathered in councils to discuss these questions and to clarify Christian teaching.",
     "In 451 AD, the Council of Chalcedon met to address disagreements about Christ.",
     "The council affirmed that Jesus Christ is one person in two natures, divine and human, without confusion or separation.",
     "However, not all Christian communities accepted the council’s wording.",
     "The church in Egypt, together with other churches, rejected the Chalcedonian definition because its leaders believed the language did not adequately express their understanding of Christ.",
     "The disagreement became part of a long and complicated history.",
     "The Coptic Orthodox Church belongs to the family of Oriental Orthodox churches, which did not accept the Council of Chalcedon.",
     "This does not mean that Coptic Christians deny the humanity or divinity of Jesus.",
