   "Topic Overview",
   "Ethiopia is home to one of the oldest Christian traditions in the world. Christianity became established in the Kingdom of Aksum during the fourth century, and the Ethiopian Orthodox Tewahedo Church has preserved its faith, worship, Scriptures, and spiritual heritage for many centuries.",
   "The story of Ethiopian Christianity reminds us that the Gospel reached Africa in the earliest centuries of the Church. Through faithful believers, courageous leaders, ancient monasteries, and generations of Christian families, the message of Jesus Christ continued to be passed down.",
   "This topic explores the biblical connection between Ethiopia and Christianity, the early Church in Ethiopia, the role of the Ethiopian Orthodox tradition, and the lessons African Christians can learn from a community that has preserved its faith through changing times.",
