   "Final Reflection — Ethiopia: A Living Witness of Ancient Christianity",
   "Ethiopia’s Christian history reminds us that the Gospel reached Africa in the earliest centuries of the Church.",
   "The biblical story of the Ethiopian official in Acts 8 shows God’s desire to reach people connected with Africa. The later history of the Kingdom of Aksum demonstrates how Christianity became established within an African kingdom.",
   "Frumentius helped strengthen the Christian community in Aksum, and the Ethiopian Orthodox Tewahedo Church continued to preserve its faith through Scripture, prayer, worship, sacred music, monasteries, and Christian teaching.",
   "The Ethiopian tradition teaches us that faith can survive through generations when believers remain committed to God’s Word and continue teaching others.",
   "It also reminds us that African Christians have played an important role in the history of the worldwide Church.",
   "As we study this heritage, we should remember that the purpose of Christian history is not simply to admire the past.",
