     "Africa has a place in the biblical story. Simon’s origin reminds us that the message of Jesus reached people from different regions and backgrounds.",
     "God can work through ordinary people. Simon is introduced simply as a man passing by, yet his action became part of the Gospel account.",
     "Discipleship begins with responding to Christ. Simon’s experience challenges believers to consider how they respond when God places an unexpected responsibility before them.",
     "The cross points us toward Jesus. Simon’s story is important because it directs our attention to the suffering and saving work of Christ."
