     "Simon’s story is brief, but its message reaches into the daily life of every believer.",
     "He came from Cyrene. He was passing by. The soldiers compelled him to carry the cross. Luke tells us that he carried it behind Jesus.",
     "These details provide a picture of an unexpected encounter with the suffering of Christ.",
     "The Gospel accounts do not tell us what happened to Simon after the crucifixion.",
     "We do not know whether he became a Christian, whether he returned to Cyrene, or whether he later shared the story with others.",
     "We should leave those questions open.",
     "But the story still teaches us important truths about following Jesus.",
     "Christian discipleship requires believers to remain attentive to God’s purposes.",
     "Sometimes the opportunity to serve appears through a planned ministry.",
     "At other times, it appears through a person who needs help, a difficult decision, or a responsibility that requires courage.",
     "Believers must learn to respond with prayer and wisdom.",
     "The story also teaches that discipleship is not about seeking recognition.",
     "Simon’s role was not presented as a public achievement or a demonstration of personal greatness.",
     "He was simply a man who carried the cross during the journey of Jesus.",
     "The attention of the Gospel remains on Christ.",
     "This is an important lesson for Christian leaders.",
     "Ministry should not become a platform for personal pride.",
